---
// SOURCE: zurp-astronomics-site — /<slug>/ product page of the main site (v2): series 2 poster on a riveted mount, worn plate sheet
// AUTHOR: engineer
// DATE: 2026-10-03
// STATUS: active
// REVISED: 2026-10-06 (ticket #49) — the page's own texts (title, status labels, titles, « based on ») come from content/
// REVISED: 2026-10-06 (ticket #66) — one licence stamp, the licence GitHub detects in the product's
//   repository, only when there is one; the site's licence rule (two stamps, a sentence) is gone
// REVISED: 2026-10-06 (ticket #75) — two stamps, each only when its licence exists: « Software · … »
//   (LICENSE, as GitHub detects it) and « Hardware · … » (LICENSE-HARDWARE, its first line)
// REVISED: 2026-10-12 (ticket #96) — the « Flash » block, only when the product's repository
//   publishes a firmware: one ESP Launchpad link per chip, named by its chip, the version flashed,
//   the whole flash erased (texts: content/site.yml, `product.flash`); `data-flash` on the block for
//   scripts/check-dist.mjs (review of #96)
// REVISED: 2026-10-12 (ticket #101) — the « Flash » block is gone with ESP Launchpad: the #install
//   block, only when the release the product installs from carries a valid installable file — the
//   ESP Web Tools button (src/components/v2/EspInstallButton.astro) on the manifest the site copies,
//   the version installed, the .hex / .img.xz links with their notice (texts: content/site.yml,
//   `product.install`); `id="install"` (a stable anchor) and `data-install` for scripts/check-dist.mjs
// REVISED: 2026-10-16 (ticket #107) — the web bench, in the #install block when the catalog holds
//   one: a button opening a near full-screen <dialog> on an <iframe allow="serial">, its `src` set
//   only when the dialog opens, and an « open in a new tab » link to the same URL (texts:
//   content/site.yml, `product.install.bench`)
// REVISED: 2026-10-20 (ticket #111) — the manual: when the product's repository writes one
//   (9_Assets/manual/), its tabs (src/components/v2/ManualTabs.astro, src/lib/manual.mjs), the
//   #install block in the Setup tab, « About » replaced by the Overview tab when there is one; the
//   tabs' behaviour in the page's script. Without a manual, the page is unchanged
//
// Content: tagline, category, badges (status, version of the latest release when there is one,
// software and hardware licences, each when there is one, based on), About, Source + repo link,
// footer. Copy from the catalog
// (src/data/catalog.ts: the product's sheet, 9_Assets/zurp.yml of its repository), word for word (it began as the v1 page's, deleted with the v1 archive in
// ticket #35); the page's own words from content/site.yml and content/catalog.yml.
//
// The licences (tickets #66, #75, the human's rules: two files of the repository, two licences) are
// the catalog's `license` (software: LICENSE, as GitHub detects it) and `hardwareLicense` (hardware:
// the first line of LICENSE-HARDWARE), stamped by src/lib/license-stamp.mjs with the texts of
// content/licences.yml: « Software · <label> », « Hardware · <label> », each only when its licence
// exists. Both keep exactly the `.badge-license` style (the « => GitHub » stamp of the home page
// copies it): they differ by an attribute, `data-licence`, which scripts/check-dist.mjs reads — no CSS
// rule of their own. A <span>, not a link: the repository is linked in the Source section, and a link
// would take the underline of the global link style. scripts/check-dist.mjs checks both stamps
// against the catalog of the build.
//
// Ticket #27: no breadcrumb any more. The site's common header (src/components/v2/SiteHeader.astro,
// drawn by V2Layout, compact and sticky on this page) carries the zUrp plate, a link to `/`, and
// the poster already says the product's name. The page's only h1 is the product name below
// (visually hidden); the header's plate is not a heading here.
import { Image, getImage } from 'astro:assets';
import V2Layout from '../../layouts/V2Layout.astro';
import { getCatalog } from '../../data/catalog';
import { accessibleFill, onAccent } from '../../lib/color';
import { catalogContent, fill, licenseContent, siteContent } from '../../lib/content.mjs';
import { licenseStamps } from '../../lib/license-stamp.mjs';
import { benchUrlPath, espManifestUrlPath } from '../../lib/install.mjs';
import EspInstallButton from '../../components/v2/EspInstallButton.astro';
import ManualTabs from '../../components/v2/ManualTabs.astro';
import { manualTabs, manualTexts } from '../../lib/manual.mjs';

export async function getStaticPaths() {
  return (await getCatalog()).map((p) => ({
    params: { slug: p.slug },
    props: { product: p },
  }));
}

const { product } = Astro.props;

const site = siteContent();
const { statuses } = catalogContent();
const licenses = licenseStamps(product, licenseContent());

// The #install block (ticket #101): present only when the product's install release carries a valid
// installable file (src/lib/catalog/install.mjs). ESP: one button for all the chips of the manifest
// (ESP Web Tools detects the chip). .hex / .img.xz: links where GitHub serves them, grouped by kind,
// each group followed by its notice. The section's `data-install`, the button's `manifest` and each
// link's `data-download` are what scripts/check-dist.mjs reads (scripts/lib/check-install.mjs): keep them.
// The web bench (ticket #107): the bench page the site copies from the same release, opened in a
// dialog over an <iframe allow="serial"> (Web Serial needs the permission in a frame; the bench is
// served from the site's own origin, src/lib/install.mjs) or in a tab. The button's `data-bench`
// (the bench's URL), the link's `data-bench-tab` and the frame's `data-bench-frame` are read by the
// same check.
const texts = site.product.install;
const install = product.install && {
  version: fill(texts.version, { tag: product.install.tag }),
  manifest: product.install.esp && espManifestUrlPath(product.slug, product.install.esp),
  bench: product.install.bench && benchUrlPath(product.slug, product.install.bench),
  groups: (['hex', 'img'] as const)
    .map((kind) => ({
      kind,
      notice: texts[kind],
      links: product.install!.downloads.filter((d) => d.kind === kind).map((d) => ({ href: d.url, text: fill(texts.download, { file: d.name }) })),
    }))
    .filter((g) => g.links.length),
};

// The manual (ticket #111): its tabs in order (null without a manual: the page as it was), the
// #install block given to ManualTabs, which places it in the Setup tab — or, without a manual, right
// where it was. The Overview tab replaces « About ».
const tabs = manualTabs(product);
const manual = tabs && manualTexts(site);
const about = !tabs?.some((t) => t.id === 'overview');

// Social cards: the series 2 poster as a JPEG. The grainy, worn print weighs more than a flat
// drawing at the same settings, hence 1000 px / q78 to stay well under the 600 KB per-image ceiling.
const ogPoster = await getImage({ src: product.poster, width: 1000, format: 'jpg', quality: 78 });

// The status badge carries text on the accent: its fill is the accent nudged (only if needed) to
// reach 4.5:1 with its text. Kaiju's red is the one that needs it; the others pass as they are.
const badge = accessibleFill(product.accent);
const tint = [
  `--z2-accent: ${product.accent}`,
  `--z2-on-accent: ${onAccent(product.accent)}`,
  `--z2-badge-fill: ${badge.fill}`,
  `--z2-on-badge: ${badge.text}`,
].join('; ');
---

<V2Layout
  title={fill(site.product.title, { product: product.name })}
  description={product.tagline}
  ogImage={ogPoster.src}
  productName={product.name}
>
  <div class="page" style={tint}>
    <!-- A <div>, not a <header>: the site header (V2Layout) is the page's one banner. -->
    <div class="hero">
      <div class="z2-container">
        <!-- The poster is the page title: it carries the name. The h1 stays for a11y / SEO. -->
        <h1 class="z2-sr-only">{product.name}</h1>

        <!-- Riveted soot mount: it absorbs the poster's opaque near-black corners, so the rays
             behind never meet the square image edge. The poster itself is never cropped. -->
        <div class="mount">
          <span class="rivet tl" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="rivet tr" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="rivet bl" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="rivet br" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <Image
            src={product.poster}
            alt={product.posterAlt}
            widths={[400, 640, 960, 1254]}
            sizes="(max-width: 720px) calc(100vw - 4rem), 660px"
            format="webp"
            quality={76}
            loading="eager"
            class="poster"
          />
        </div>

        <p class="category">{product.category.toUpperCase()}</p>

        <div class="badges">
          <span class={`badge badge-${product.status}`}>{statuses[product.status].label}</span>
          {product.release && <span class="badge badge-version">{product.release.tag}</span>}
          {licenses.software && <span class="badge badge-license" data-licence="software" title={licenses.software.title ?? undefined}>{licenses.software.text}</span>}
          {licenses.hardware && <span class="badge badge-license" data-licence="hardware" title={licenses.hardware.title ?? undefined}>{licenses.hardware.text}</span>}
          {product.basedOn && <span class="badge badge-based">{fill(site.product.basedOn, { basedOn: product.basedOn })}</span>}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <main class="z2-container">
      <div class="sheet z2-plate">
        <section class="lead">
          <p class="pitch">{product.tagline}</p>
        </section>

        {about && (
          <section class="description">
            <h2 class="z2-band">{site.product.aboutTitle}</h2>
            {product.description.map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}
          </section>
        )}

        <ManualTabs tabs={tabs} texts={manual} product={product.name}>
        {install && (
          <section class="install" id="install" data-install>
            <h2 class="z2-band">{texts.title}</h2>
            <p class="install-version">{install.version}</p>
            {install.manifest && (
              <div class="install-esp">
                <p>{texts.esp.intro}</p>
                <EspInstallButton manifest={install.manifest} label={texts.esp.button} />
              </div>
            )}
            {install.groups.map((g) => (
              <div class="install-download">
                <ul class="install-links">
                  {g.links.map((l) => (
                    <li>
                      <a class="repo-link" href={l.href} data-download={g.kind}>
                        <span class="repo-icon" aria-hidden="true">{site.product.sourceArrow}</span>
                        <span class="repo-url">{l.text}</span>
                      </a>
                    </li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
                <p>{g.notice}</p>
              </div>
            ))}
            {install.bench && (
              <div class="install-bench">
                <p>{texts.bench.intro}</p>
                <div class="bench-actions">
                  <button type="button" class="bench-open" data-bench={install.bench} aria-haspopup="dialog">{texts.bench.button}</button>
                  <a class="repo-link" href={install.bench} target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-bench-tab>
                    <span class="repo-icon" aria-hidden="true">{site.product.sourceArrow}</span>
                    <span class="repo-url">{texts.bench.tab}</span>
                  </a>
                </div>
                <dialog class="bench-dialog" data-bench-dialog aria-label={fill(texts.bench.frame, { product: product.name })}>
                  <form method="dialog" class="bench-bar">
                    <button class="bench-close">{texts.bench.close}</button>
                  </form>
                  <iframe allow="serial" title={fill(texts.bench.frame, { product: product.name })} data-bench-frame></iframe>
                </dialog>
              </div>
            )}
          </section>
        )}
        </ManualTabs>

        <section class="repo">
          <h2 class="z2-band">{site.product.sourceTitle}</h2>
          <a class="repo-link" href={product.repo}>
            <span class="repo-icon" aria-hidden="true">{site.product.sourceArrow}</span>
            <span class="repo-url">{product.repo.replace('https://github.com/', 'github.com/')}</span>
          </a>
        </section>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
</V2Layout>

<script>
  // The bench dialog (ticket #107). Nothing loads before the click: the frame has no `src` until the
  // dialog opens. Closed (its close button, a <form method="dialog">, or Escape, native to a modal
  // <dialog>), the frame is emptied: the bench page unloads and gives the serial port back, so that
  // the « new tab » link, or the next opening, can take it (a port is open in one page at a time).
  for (const open of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button[data-bench]')) {
    const dialog = open.closest('.install-bench')?.querySelector<HTMLDialogElement>('dialog[data-bench-dialog]');
    const frame = dialog?.querySelector<HTMLIFrameElement>('iframe[data-bench-frame]');
    if (!dialog || !frame) continue;
    open.addEventListener('click', () => {
      frame.src = open.dataset.bench!;
      dialog.showModal();
    });
    dialog.addEventListener('close', () => {
      frame.src = 'about:blank';
    });
  }

  // The manual's tabs (ticket #111, src/components/v2/ManualTabs.astro): the WAI-ARIA tabs pattern
  // with automatic activation — a click or an arrow key shows its panel; Left / Right move between
  // the tabs (wrapping), Home / End go to the first / last; only the selected tab is in the Tab order.
  // An anchor opens the panel that holds it: a tab's own (`#setup`), or anything inside a panel
  // (`#install`, in Setup), at load and at every change of the anchor (a manual's link to another
  // tab is one); without one, the first tab. Choosing a tab writes its anchor in the address, without
  // scrolling, so that it can be shared.
  for (const manual of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-manual]')) {
    const tabs = [...manual.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[role="tab"]')];
    const panels = tabs.map((t) => document.getElementById(t.getAttribute('aria-controls') ?? ''));
    if (!tabs.length || panels.some((p) => !p)) continue;
    const select = (i: number) =>
      tabs.forEach((tab, j) => {
        tab.setAttribute('aria-selected', String(i === j));
        tab.tabIndex = i === j ? 0 : -1;
        panels[j]!.hidden = i !== j;
      });
    const choose = (i: number) => {
      select(i);
      history.replaceState(null, '', `#${panels[i]!.id}`);
    };
    const open = (hash: string) => {
      let id = '';
      try {
        id = decodeURIComponent(hash.replace(/^#/, ''));
      } catch {
        return false;
      }
      const target = id ? document.getElementById(id) : null;
      const i = target ? panels.findIndex((p) => p!.contains(target)) : -1;
      if (i < 0) return false;
      select(i);
      (target === panels[i] ? manual : target)!.scrollIntoView();
      return true;
    };
    tabs.forEach((tab, i) => tab.addEventListener('click', () => choose(i)));
    manual.querySelector('[role="tablist"]')?.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
      const e = event as KeyboardEvent;
      const at = tabs.indexOf(document.activeElement as HTMLButtonElement);
      const to = ({ ArrowRight: at + 1, ArrowLeft: at - 1, Home: 0, End: tabs.length - 1 } as Record<string, number>)[e.key];
      if (at < 0 || to === undefined) return;
      e.preventDefault();
      const i = (to + tabs.length) % tabs.length;
      choose(i);
      tabs[i].focus();
    });
    window.addEventListener('hashchange', () => open(location.hash));
    if (!open(location.hash)) select(0);
  }
</script>

<style>
  /* Top padding: the gap under the common header's hairline (the breadcrumb that used to sit
     here is gone, ticket #27). */
  .hero {
    position: relative;
    isolation: isolate;
    padding: 2.5rem 0 2.5rem;
    text-align: center;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* Accent rays fanning out behind the mount, worn down by a halftone screen. Masked (not painted
     over) so they fade into the wall itself instead of ending on a flat soot edge. */
  .hero::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: -1;
    background:
      var(--z2-halftone),
      repeating-conic-gradient(
        from 4deg at 50% 44%,
        color-mix(in srgb, var(--z2-accent) 55%, transparent) 0deg 8deg,
        transparent 8deg 30deg
      );
    -webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse 70% 62% at 50% 44%, #000 30%, transparent 80%);
    mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse 70% 62% at 50% 44%, #000 30%, transparent 80%);
  }

  .mount {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto 2rem;
    padding: 20px;
    border-radius: 26px;
    /* Flat, and exactly the poster's corner black: the image's square edge must not show. */
    background: var(--z2-soot);
    box-shadow:
      inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(236, 223, 191, 0.1),
      0 0 0 3px var(--z2-soot-deep),
      0 0 0 6px color-mix(in srgb, var(--z2-accent) 80%, black),
      14px 16px 0 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
  }

  .rivet {
    position: absolute;
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: radial-gradient(circle at 35% 35%, #8d877c, #3a3631 60%, #1a1816);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.8);
  }

  .rivet.tl { top: 6px; left: 6px; }
  .rivet.tr { top: 6px; right: 6px; }
  .rivet.bl { bottom: 6px; left: 6px; }
  .rivet.br { bottom: 6px; right: 6px; }

  /* Square, whole poster — never cropped. The 5 % radius only trims its dark outer margin. */
  .poster {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    border-radius: 5%;
  }

  .category {
    font-family: var(--z2-font-body);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-stretch: 125%;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.3em;
    color: var(--z2-cream);
    margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
  }

  .badges {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  /* Rubber stamps: slightly crooked, inked unevenly. */
  .badge {
    position: relative;
    font-family: var(--z2-font-type);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    padding: 0.3rem 0.8rem 0.2rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    border: 2px solid currentColor;
    border-radius: 4px;
    transform: rotate(-1.5deg);
  }

  .badge:nth-child(2) {
    transform: rotate(1deg);
  }

  .badge:nth-child(3) {
    transform: rotate(-0.5deg);
  }

  .badge:nth-child(4) {
    transform: rotate(0.8deg);
  }

  /* Fill and text from accessibleFill() (≥ 4.5:1); the outer ring keeps the true accent. */
  .badge-wip {
    background: var(--z2-badge-fill);
    color: var(--z2-on-badge);
    border-color: var(--z2-soot-deep);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--z2-accent);
  }

  .badge-future {
    background: var(--z2-soot-deep);
    color: var(--z2-cream);
    border-color: var(--z2-accent);
  }

  .badge-released {
    background: #2f9e44;
    color: var(--z2-cream-light);
    border-color: var(--z2-soot-deep);
  }

  /* The version (ticket #46): the tag of the latest GitHub release, as is, only when there is one.
     Inked on soot like the licence stamp, with a dashed rim in the product's accent; the tag keeps
     its own case. */
  .badge-version {
    background: var(--z2-soot-deep);
    color: var(--z2-cream);
    border-color: var(--z2-accent);
    border-style: dashed;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: none;
  }

  .badge-license,
  .badge-based {
    background: rgba(16, 15, 14, 0.7);
    color: var(--z2-cream);
    border-style: double;
    border-width: 4px;
  }

  .sheet {
    margin: 2.5rem auto 0;
    max-width: 900px;
    padding: 0 2.25rem 0.5rem;
    border-top: 0;
  }

  /* Accent band across the top of the plate, scuffed by the halftone. */
  .sheet::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 22px;
    right: 22px;
    height: 10px;
    background: var(--z2-halftone), var(--z2-accent);
    border-radius: 0 0 4px 4px;
  }

  section {
    padding: 2.5rem 0;
  }

  section + section,
  :global(.manual) + section {
    border-top: 2px dashed rgba(74, 64, 51, 0.55);
  }

  /* An anchor (#install) scrolls it under the sticky header of product pages, not behind it. */
  .install {
    scroll-margin-top: 7rem;
  }

  section h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 5vw, 2.6rem);
    margin-bottom: 1.6rem;
    margin-left: -0.15rem;
  }

  .lead {
    padding-top: 3rem;
  }

  .lead .pitch {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    max-width: 680px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--z2-ink);
  }

  .description p {
    color: var(--z2-ink);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .install p {
    color: var(--z2-ink);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .install .install-version {
    font-family: var(--z2-font-type);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }

  .install-esp,
  .install-download {
    margin-top: 1.4rem;
  }

  .install-esp p {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .install-bench {
    margin-top: 1.4rem;
  }

  .install-bench p {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .bench-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: stretch;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .bench-open,
  .bench-close {
    cursor: pointer;
    border: 0;
    background: var(--z2-accent);
    color: var(--z2-on-accent);
    font-family: var(--z2-font-type);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }

  .bench-open {
    padding: 0.95rem 1.6rem 0.85rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    box-shadow: 6px 6px 0 rgba(29, 26, 22, 0.35);
    transition: transform 0.15s ease, box-shadow 0.15s ease;
  }

  .bench-open:hover {
    transform: translate(-2px, -2px);
    box-shadow: 8px 8px 0 rgba(29, 26, 22, 0.45);
  }

  .bench-open:focus-visible,
  .bench-close:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid var(--z2-ink);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  /* Near full screen (95vw × 90vh, Basilisk's measure of what its bench needs). */
  .bench-dialog {
    width: 95vw;
    height: 90vh;
    max-width: none;
    max-height: none;
    margin: auto;
    padding: 0;
    border: 3px solid var(--z2-soot-deep);
    background: var(--z2-soot-deep);
  }

  .bench-dialog[open] {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .bench-dialog::backdrop {
    background: rgba(16, 15, 14, 0.75);
  }

  .bench-bar {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    padding: 0.4rem;
  }

  .bench-close {
    padding: 0.55rem 1.1rem 0.45rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .bench-dialog iframe {
    flex: 1;
    width: 100%;
    border: 0;
    background: var(--z2-cream-light);
  }

  .install-links {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .repo-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: stretch;
    max-width: 100%;
    background: var(--z2-soot-deep);
    color: var(--z2-cream);
    font-family: var(--z2-font-type);
